id: pm-rust-native-capabilities
title: Discover exact native command and SDK contracts in one bounded call
description: "Versioned native flags, output dimensions, backend operations and typed recovery schemas with explicit oracle slices and native-only evidence."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: contracts,discovery,"gh:unbraind/pm-rust#148",native
created_at: "2026-11-04T22:32:15.530Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T03:44:35.257Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Every advertised operation has a real invocation or parity receipt; unsupported methods cannot appear available; one bounded discovery call replaces multi-command help reads; no Git or Node runtime; typed SDK and compact TOON/JSON CLI with remedies; read-only public-copy validation; exact-head npm/Bun release gates.
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T22:32:58.236Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against current pm 2026.11.4 contracts output, the pinned 2026.10.21 public SDK capability/flag contracts, pm-web contract-explorer.ts, native-adapter ABI and bounded read sessions. Upstream describes the host command/runtime surface; pm-web projects provider availability; the ABI grants transport operations; sessions bound results. None inventories the compiled native product. This feature will derive exact flags from the real Clap parser, declare only evidenced native operation slices, and report injected backends as unavailable unless explicitly supplied and validated. No import/export/sync, tracker mutation, journal, shared lease or status interpretation is added. Existing SDK readers/codecs and adapter validators remain authoritative. Unsupported native options and methods default to unavailable; the oracle version labels evidence, never inferred compatibility."
  "2026-11-04T22:45:14.204Z",codex-agent,"Implemented shared parser-derived discovery plus typed request/refusal/response contracts and complete bounded native TOON/JSON encodings. Initial targeted validation passes 8 tests: 5 schema/parser/backend/output units and 3 native integration tests, including every advertised command invoked on a genuine non-git tracker, 500 seeded randomized request/replay sequences comparing unchanged SDK-read item state, and 500 numeric-boundary fuzz cases. All 32 adapter grant subsets are checked without opening a transport. The read-only feature adds no imports/exports/sync, journaled plans, retry keys, status-role decisions or shared mutable state; those existing paths are unchanged. A round-trip regression caught list-specific TOON table projection, so discovery uses the native codec directly and both producers now round-trip the same typed response."
  "2026-11-04T22:59:24.637Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert passed: replacing only discover_capabilities with an unsupported-operation refusal in a disposable non-git copy compiles successfully and makes discovery_is_complete_bounded_and_tracker_free fail by assertion (0 passed, 1 failed). The reviewed source was untouched. Fixed-source verification follows the proof. The three linked pm test commands passed: 6 discovery units, 3 native contract tests and 17 existing CLI dispatch tests (26 total). Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so these receipts are recorded here without changing project settings. The Rust get command is explicitly classified as a native-only flat document projection rather than implying host entity-envelope parity. No new SDK gap or upstream defect was identified."
  "2026-11-04T23:12:48.495Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence: 27 targeted passes across the linked 6 discovery units, 3 native contract tests, 17 existing dispatch tests and 1 writer/flush test; both seeded models run 500 cases. Added explicit inventory-drift, codec-failure and JSON-fits/TOON-refuses recovery checks. Current clippy all-targets/all-features, strict Rust docs, TypeScript, ESLint and format checks pass. The refined function-only behavioral revert again compiles and fails the acceptance assertion; the fixed tracker-free test passes after restoration. Read-only public main a4e9e18 validates 94 SDK-certified items, 201 authoritative files including 7 SDK preparation files, 7088848 bytes and 129 native calls. Inventory: 25 operations, 236 argument contracts, 17 oracle slices and 8 native-only surfaces; JSON 55534 bytes, TOON 66215 bytes, largest selected JSON 9528 bytes, 3848 ms measured wall time. SDK complete item/body/relationship read-back and frozen fingerprint agree. Aggregate receipt and commands are linked in docs. Final full npm/Bun release gates remain the unchanged CI workflow; exact-head results will be recorded in the PR so a later tracker write cannot invalidate verification. Releasing only this author claim and retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification; no close, merge or product release."
  "2026-11-04T23:25:26.575Z",codex-agent,"While exact-head CI was queued, focused source inspection identified one unreachable CLI render-error region after successful discovery admission. Refine the delivery boundary so unexpected invalid typed responses, codec failures and writer failures share explicit exercised refusal handling. Discovery data and schemas are unchanged. This is a targeted coverage/correctness follow-up on the same item; final-head CI will be refreshed after the fix."
  "2026-11-04T23:30:31.769Z",codex-agent,"Delivery refinement verified: unexpected over-budget typed responses emit no bytes; write and flush failures remain failures; source inspection shows the added dispatch/delivery regions exercised. Both independent function-only controls compile and fail their selected runtime assertions: disabled discovery fails tracker-free acceptance, and false-success CLI delivery fails the writer-refusal test. Both fixed-source tests pass afterward. The full public-copy validator passes again with identical discovery bytes and operation counts; refreshed aggregate timing/fingerprint is committed. Strict all-target Rust lint, TypeScript, ESLint, format and changelog checks are retained. Releasing this claim again; the final corrective commit requires fresh exact-head CI, and gate results remain in the PR."
  "2026-11-04T23:58:51.257Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK output-bound audit found that a caller-modified/deserialized DiscoveryResponse could raise its output_bytes above the documented hard ceiling before calling render. Enforce the same numeric domain inside rendering, before encoding, and add received-metadata extreme-value coverage. Normal discovery output is unchanged. This closes an output-boundary contract on the same item; final release gates must target the resulting new head."
  "2026-11-05T00:03:45.638Z",codex-agent,"Renderer hard ceiling fixed before encoding. The new received-metadata regression compiled and failed against the unchanged original render function (0 passed, 1 failed), then all 7 discovery units passed with the guard, including both 500-case models in their targeted coverage scope. PM-linked discovery tests pass again. Focused final discovery-source coverage is 100 percent: 605 lines, 44 functions, 607 regions and 48 branch outcomes. All-target clippy, strict Rust docs, the final native build/SDK example and full read-only public-copy validator pass; 25 operations, 236 arguments, 94 items and 129 native calls retain identical discovery bytes. Refreshed aggregate numbers and fingerprint are committed. The prescribed CI wait window elapsed before release certification finished; prior-head CI results do not certify this final hardening commit. The PR will identify the fresh final-head run and pending npm/Bun gates. Releasing this author claim; retain in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-05T00:08:50.128Z",codex-agent,"Final-source linked acceptance rerun passed all four commands with zero skipped selections: 7 discovery units, 3 native contract tests, 17 existing CLI dispatch tests and 1 delivery test, 28 total. Clarification of the preceding note: the 500-case numeric model is in the unit set; the separate 500-sequence request/replay and SDK state-preservation model is in the integration set. Both were rerun successfully on the final renderer guard. All tracker writes are now complete before the final CI refresh. Global npm/Bun release certification remains pending and must not be inferred from component coverage or earlier heads."
  "2026-11-05T02:29:52.937Z",codex-agent,"Review round on 962997b: fetched all five unresolved threads and all comments (no pagination remaining). Latest CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range findings; its session refusal producer test nit is also valid. Plan: isolate revert build artifacts, enforce object-only discovery inputs, include lifecycle wrapper SDK entry points, filter both backend operation lists with the selected operation, correct JSON-only ownership encodings, and add actual session producer coverage. Prove regressions in disposable copies, self-review the full PR, and run unchanged just release-check with two build jobs and two test threads. Remote branch is current and includes main."
  "2026-11-05T02:36:15.110Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all five valid thread fixes and the session producer comparison nit. Self-review of the complete PR also corrected positional arrays at both adapter input boundaries, injected-adapter operation filtering, and claim/release option-dependent public SDK entry points. The moved parser definitions match main after visibility, crate qualification and the documented discovery addition are normalized. Focused discovery units: 10 passed. Runner artifact boundary: 4 passed, including absent/existing executable and both runner failure paths. All-target clippy, TypeScript and ESLint passed. Revert controls run only in an owned disposable copy with an isolated Cargo target; the reviewed source and its compiled executable remain untouched."
  "2026-11-05T02:45:13.378Z",codex-agent,"Revert evidence: node scripts/native-adapter-capabilities-review-revert.mts independently compiled nine function-only controls; each produced 0 passed and 1 assertion failure, never a compilation or launch failure. Controls: request object admission (thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6z3lA3), nested-adapter and CLI-adapter object admission, lifecycle wrapper mapping (PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6z3lBH), claim option mapping, local backend filtering (PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6z3lBQ), injected-adapter filtering, ownership JSON-only encodings (PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6z3lBT), and session descriptor rename (review-body nit). The separate artifact control reintroduced the shared Cargo target and failed the runner artifact tests (PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6z3lAx); the fixed runner tests pass all 4 cases. An initial harness copy omitted an existing example fixture and stopped at compilation; that attempt is excluded from revert evidence. Final restored-source reruns are running. Public-copy validator passed 94 certified items, 25 operations, 236 argument contracts and 129 native calls, with identical CLI/SDK inventory and unchanged tracker state; receipt refreshed. No unresolved finding was rejected and no out-of-scope defect or SDK gap was identified."
  "2026-11-05T02:46:54.472Z",codex-agent,"All restored-source regressions pass after the independent reverts: 10 discovery units and 5 real CLI contract tests; runner artifact tests pass 4 cases. Starting the unchanged full Rust aggregate with two Cargo build jobs and two Rust test threads. Optional tracker health preflight detected existing extension host version skew; recorded it on existing follow-up pm-rust-vuwe and reinstalled the pinned checkout merge drivers without changing the dependency pins or history records."
  "2026-11-05T03:34:08.999Z",codex-agent,"Unchanged local just release-check: formatting, all-target clippy and strict docs passed; 607 tests passed and one existing orientation budget-floor case hit its native child deadline. The exact failing case then passed on retry with the original 5-second deadline and --test-threads=2 (1 passed, 0 failed), matching existing follow-up pm-rust-local-packet-deadline. The aggregate stopped before its coverage/security phases, so this is not a full local gate pass. Prior-head CI 41939289764 separately identified one uncovered region at write_discovery_to producer-refusal propagation (main.rs:110); added a direct typed-refusal/no-output test for both encodings without changing thresholds or production semantics. Its focused test passes. Extended disposable controls to prove that replacing a producer refusal with successful rediscovery fails this new assertion. Fresh final-head CI must certify the complete aggregate; earlier component coverage is not full-repository certification."
  "2026-11-05T03:43:34.500Z",codex-agent,"Final disposable controls passed: all 11 independent negatives detected their intended defect, including 10 successfully compiled Rust controls with exactly 0 passed/1 failed each, plus the shared-target artifact control. The additional producer-refusal control replaces Err with successful rediscovery and fails capabilities_writer_refusals; restored-source reruns pass 10 discovery units, 5 CLI contract tests and 1 writer test. All five fetched review threads are valid and addressed, including adjacent adapter/SDK/filter instances; no thread replies or resolutions were made. Local unchanged aggregate receipt remains 607 passed plus one existing deadline failure, resolved by an unchanged focused retry (1 passed). Cargo audit exits 0 with the existing allowed unsafe-libyaml maintenance warning. Crash harness currently has 43 passing cases and continues unchanged. The final-head full aggregate and remaining local runtime receipts will be recorded on PR 148 so subsequent tracker writes cannot invalidate the certified head. Releasing only this author claim; keep feature in_progress for orchestrator verification. Existing health host/extension version skew remains tracked on pm-rust-vuwe; dependency pins and append-only history are preserved."
  "2026-11-05T03:44:35.254Z",codex-agent,"Final local crash-check completed successfully: 86 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped, 0 cancelled, 0 todo. TypeScript and ESLint, append-only history-prefix validation and retained-evidence commit validation also pass. The four new executable-isolation regressions are included in this full 86-case harness run. Cargo audit and canonical changelog checks pass; the full aggregate remains for fresh pushed-head CI because its local first pass stopped at the already resolved load-related deadline. All implementation and tracker changes will be committed together; final-head CI receipts remain external on PR 148. This author claim is already released and the feature remains in_progress."
